./docs/mcp.md-2-
./docs/mcp.md-3-DevX provides a local Model Context Protocol server over stdio. It lets an MCP client use the current working directory as its repository, with a local SQLite session created when the server starts. The server is local only: it has no authentication or network listener.
./docs/mcp.md-4-
./docs/mcp.md-5-Start it from the repository you want to work with:
./docs/mcp.md-6-
./docs/mcp.md:7:```sh
./docs/mcp.md-8-devx mcp serve
./docs/mcp.md:9:```
./docs/mcp.md-10-
./docs/mcp.md-11-The transport uses newline-delimited JSON-RPC 2.0 on stdin and stdout; diagnostics belong on stderr. The repository session is created for each server process. The server does not index automatically at startup. If an index-dependent tool is called before the repository has indexed files, it returns `isError: true` with this text: “repository not indexed: call the `index` tool first (omit `files` to index the whole repository)”. Call `index` first to build the index.
