./docs/reporting.md-11-
./docs/reporting.md-12-Export 60 days when comparing a current 30-day period to the preceding 30 days. Exports contain workspace-namespaced event IDs, optional history windows and current index-health snapshots. Repeated IDs are deduplicated. Sessionless calls are included in local exports; separate worktrees remain separate workspace rows even when repository names coincide. Output files are created exclusively: choose a new destination rather than overwriting an existing artifact.
./docs/reporting.md-13-
./docs/reporting.md-14-Existing JSON fields remain unchanged for compatibility. `Reporting.Availability` and the new metric objects supply collection states. `ZERO` means collected with zero observations; `COLLECTED` accompanies a positive value; `NOT COLLECTED` means an existing source supplied no measurement for this period; `UNAVAILABLE` means no implemented source. The last two have null values and never display as zero. Existing numeric JSON counters are legacy fields; consumers needing coverage must use the additive states, not infer availability from those counters.
./docs/reporting.md-15-
--
./docs/reporting.md-23-
./docs/reporting.md-24-## Optional harness integration
./docs/reporting.md-25-
./docs/reporting.md-26-`fallback observe` records an observation without executing the shell command:
./docs/reporting.md-27-
./docs/reporting.md:28:```sh
./docs/reporting.md-29-devx fallback observe --session "$SESSION_ID" --agent deepseek --command 'rg people db.py'
./docs/reporting.md-30-devx fallback observe --session "$SESSION_ID" --agent deepseek --command 'cat logs/server.log'
./docs/reporting.md-31-devx fallback observe --session "$SESSION_ID" --agent deepseek --command 'cat db.py | head'
./docs/reporting.md:32:```
./docs/reporting.md-33-
./docs/reporting.md-34-The classifications are `bypass candidate` for indexed source/docs in this repository, `allowed` for logs/build/generated/non-indexed files, and `unclassified` for piped or unknown scope. A candidate is not a confirmed policy violation. Complex shell syntax is intentionally not interpreted. A harness can provide repeated `--file <path>` operands for simple commands when it knows their scope.
./docs/reporting.md-35-
./docs/reporting.md-36-An example Claude Code PreToolUse adapter is [tools/devx-pretooluse.py.example](../tools/devx-pretooluse.py.example). It runs with Python despite the example suffix; the suffix avoids adding a Python runtime target to a .NET repository. Opt in through your own harness configuration; DevX does not install or activate it. Supply `DEVX_ROOT`, `DEVX_SESSION`, and the brief's `DEVX_AGENT` label. For a Bash PreToolUse hook, invoke:
./docs/reporting.md-37-
./docs/reporting.md:38:```sh
./docs/reporting.md-39-python3 /absolute/path/to/devx/tools/devx-pretooluse.py.example
./docs/reporting.md:40:```
./docs/reporting.md-41-
./docs/reporting.md-42-The adapter requires DevX 1.5.0. `DEVX_EXECUTABLE` can point to an isolated candidate CLI for testing without replacing the global tool. It records tool requests, not proof that the command completed. The adapter writes observations only. The harness must separately report completed intervals during which it knows the hook was enabled for that session/agent:
./docs/reporting.md-43-
./docs/reporting.md:44:```sh
./docs/reporting.md-45-devx fallback observe --session "$SESSION_ID" --agent deepseek \
./docs/reporting.md-46-  --coverage-start 2026-10-07T10:00:00Z --coverage-end 2026-10-07T10:15:00Z
./docs/reporting.md:47:```
./docs/reporting.md-48-
./docs/reporting.md-49-Do not claim a future interval or an entire session just because one callback fired. Reports clip supplied spans to the reporting period. No observations with coverage off is NOT COLLECTED, never compliance. Observation events without intervals remain visible but have no continuous-coverage claim. Telemetry and completed spans are self-reported, not tamper-proof audit data; shell aliases and tools outside the observed harness remain invisible. Hook failures are non-blocking and print NOT COLLECTED to stderr.
./docs/reporting.md-50-
./docs/reporting.md-51-Shell command text, attempted names and failure reasons may contain sensitive content. Observation is opt-in; review exports before sharing and do not pass secrets in observed commands. No telemetry is uploaded.
./docs/reporting.md-52-
